WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.671
JAMIE: How is that a Wall Street story
and not just a startup

00:00:02.671 --> 00:00:05.342
JAMIE: tragedy story?

00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:09.251
RUFUS: Because the question those
analysts are asking is: what does this
tell

00:00:09.251 --> 00:00:13.075
RUFUS: us about Meta's data strategy?
Sundial built what they called "agentic
analysts"

00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:16.899
RUFUS: — AI agents that could
autonomously clean messy data and
surface insights,

00:00:16.899 --> 00:00:20.723
RUFUS: through tools like Slack. Picture
a junior analyst who never sleeps and

00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:24.547
RUFUS: doesn't complain about
spreadsheet formatting.

00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:26.065
ALEX: Back to the wider story.

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:28.426
RUFUS: Meta just bought that person and
told everyone else they can't hire

00:00:28.426 --> 00:00:30.676
RUFUS: them anymore.

00:00:30.889 --> 00:00:35.004
JAMIE: And Sundial had raised twenty-
three million dollars before this.
